frac{5\\pi }{12}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-87125/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75c0168a-efdc-5162-a961-aae318783e50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-87125"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8616"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/e76766c18330d476af9253ecb2d08540df06146a9ac2fdc6bfbe6f8157201f6b.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the ray shown above?" :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection/b3f521bd26b4522eb4f6d6d57d607122e9b9055971c7867bae7056965ddddd4e" :answer/id #uuid "ca0b6e2e-d5f6-5011-a6f6-23255aceb737" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection/8390c894ce4519f409cfead6227ba86a45861054a4cf82b899ab16af91f98a54" :answer/id #uuid "65875231-4f54-52ac-b385-fc009f009658" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection/f73056dace33dcd70785663113de5f7bbe6a9cac9aa8eeaa4fd8814fa94f13c2" :answer/id #uuid "13d551bd-34a0-52a5-a934-1b577b5f88db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection/a655fd8a8ec1a2a4cdab514feb8c54ac135e02c514c9a666447c07942d90d267" :answer/id #uuid "e8755f11-0af7-545c-ad3c-f7b1dbd4317f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{9\\pi }{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection/089718ed8dc5ea9b467ab719297063e2734ec62dd7dd39cff1ae338c7e8c45a4" :answer/id #uuid "d9cba7a3-3874-5e3a-999a-faf4f0147f4a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{13\\pi }{15}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "d06d2ad3-c9d2-5285-a8c6-d86951e0d0f6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-120653/selection/f73056dace33dcd70785663113de5f7bbe6a9cac9aa8eeaa4fd8814fa94f13c2" :answer-field/choices ["q-120653/selection/b3f521bd26b4522eb4f6d6d57d607122e9b9055971c7867bae7056965ddddd4e" "q-120653/selection/8390c894ce4519f409cfead6227ba86a45861054a4cf82b899ab16af91f98a54" "q-120653/selection/f73056dace33dcd70785663113de5f7bbe6a9cac9aa8eeaa4fd8814fa94f13c2" "q-120653/selection/a655fd8a8ec1a2a4cdab514feb8c54ac135e02c514c9a666447c07942d90d267" "q-120653/selection/089718ed8dc5ea9b467ab719297063e2734ec62dd7dd39cff1ae338c7e8c45a4"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-120653" :question/id #uuid "a7f4889a-ead3-5e37-b2a3-e29f54239e95" :question/math-academy-id "q-120653" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/d52d7a1e64de7618d5c9253ee00eafc43462e8a40e52fa7da671ef1f5a094e68.png)\n\nWhat is the polar equation of the ray shown above?" :question/worked-solution "The counterclockwise angle that the ray makes with the positive $x$-axis is\n\n$$\n\\pi -\\frac{8\\pi }{15}=\\frac{7\\pi }{15}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is $\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{15}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-120653/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "75c0168a-efdc-5162-a961-aae318783e50"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-120653"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection/92ed4dc763639740991b294b2e716df07a62a010be23a205b4128998a6035ea6" :answer/id #uuid "c4822ac9-1eaa-53b5-b4f4-cd76a1d72973" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection/c3f1b2278971eee7a6c21dfe4d389816019b5ed3a9949fb44d8116125acd5842" :answer/id #uuid "21e85f79-2a92-5bf7-8844-d2d4a3ffc72f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection/004b40e9dbf8f036600a30e235f0e875769fd38731126675bdaffac624ba888c" :answer/id #uuid "58e4031b-29b2-52fe-9477-45a81cd5cda0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{11\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection/9d4d1c66e82dbe006fc485d871e23727a78e849470fa0546d1e250098f1ba0f7" :answer/id #uuid "36979e07-cf9c-5b5f-9024-acb342620044" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection/7e2b48383d5d1cc80a4b40001f958af2e676fec2cb1400c3d40af53d8105a997" :answer/id #uuid "ab41cbf5-c9a7-5e7c-8d18-a93c055845bd" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "34689735-8a28-52f5-b1ca-c3b57b5a59e1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-40913/selection/9d4d1c66e82dbe006fc485d871e23727a78e849470fa0546d1e250098f1ba0f7" :answer-field/choices ["q-40913/selection/92ed4dc763639740991b294b2e716df07a62a010be23a205b4128998a6035ea6" "q-40913/selection/c3f1b2278971eee7a6c21dfe4d389816019b5ed3a9949fb44d8116125acd5842" "q-40913/selection/004b40e9dbf8f036600a30e235f0e875769fd38731126675bdaffac624ba888c" "q-40913/selection/9d4d1c66e82dbe006fc485d871e23727a78e849470fa0546d1e250098f1ba0f7" "q-40913/selection/7e2b48383d5d1cc80a4b40001f958af2e676fec2cb1400c3d40af53d8105a997"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-40913" :question/id #uuid "b2490317-067b-513c-9277-23bae0b21e71" :question/math-academy-id "q-40913" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/19f94b8985a4b8da7899f984e0e1c3f88668aa59531658cd0118edb35aab1107.png)\n\nGiven that the ray above passes through the point with Cartesian coordinates $(-6,-2\\sqrt{3})$, find the polar equation of the ray." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-2\\sqrt{3}}{-6}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{3}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the third quadrant. So, we find the angle in the third quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-40913/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d90b9572-cdac-51f7-b386-81b750642585"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-40913"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection/7e2b48383d5d1cc80a4b40001f958af2e676fec2cb1400c3d40af53d8105a997" :answer/id #uuid "bc830c5b-fe18-5dbf-ac4e-f7b8c5a9315d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection/8390c894ce4519f409cfead6227ba86a45861054a4cf82b899ab16af91f98a54" :answer/id #uuid "020f1180-8560-5ae8-8ac6-1f89bc6fc69b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection/085377617428ca5593e1c4521bc89fb219cb72bde070d1b7a71c3ae7e00e1c0b" :answer/id #uuid "895369e6-c16e-5d29-969e-446a6c49885d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{2\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection/92ed4dc763639740991b294b2e716df07a62a010be23a205b4128998a6035ea6" :answer/id #uuid "5158bbeb-ba70-50b3-8da6-8b415b43f5eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection/c3f1b2278971eee7a6c21dfe4d389816019b5ed3a9949fb44d8116125acd5842" :answer/id #uuid "c11d7e5c-bc8f-5de0-a2f6-d8cc1cc06db0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\theta =\\frac{4\\pi }{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e0b41517-9d29-5c76-bdc3-9114bb649974" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-17161/selection/92ed4dc763639740991b294b2e716df07a62a010be23a205b4128998a6035ea6" :answer-field/choices ["q-17161/selection/7e2b48383d5d1cc80a4b40001f958af2e676fec2cb1400c3d40af53d8105a997" "q-17161/selection/8390c894ce4519f409cfead6227ba86a45861054a4cf82b899ab16af91f98a54" "q-17161/selection/085377617428ca5593e1c4521bc89fb219cb72bde070d1b7a71c3ae7e00e1c0b" "q-17161/selection/92ed4dc763639740991b294b2e716df07a62a010be23a205b4128998a6035ea6" "q-17161/selection/c3f1b2278971eee7a6c21dfe4d389816019b5ed3a9949fb44d8116125acd5842"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-17161" :question/id #uuid "88a106f3-b03f-57fc-a519-6c763e438e5c" :question/math-academy-id "q-17161" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/11a75207b0adee9fad857aa93f15772e730716b7cc9d5fae7ba39fc5f55418f0.png)\n\nGiven that the ray above passes through the point with Cartesian coordinates $(5,-5\\sqrt{3})$, find the polar equation of the ray." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-5\\sqrt{3}}{5}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡\\sqrt{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the fourth quadrant. So, we find the angle in the fourth quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{3},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =2\\pi -{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =2\\pi -\\frac{\\pi }{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{5\\pi }{3}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-17161/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d90b9572-cdac-51f7-b386-81b750642585"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-17161"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321898/field-1/0a6ddc2b5a7aa53dbaf860b36b1154868d90594d50efab51f97b669902110496" :answer/id #uuid "4f845f32-0b5d-5d33-85cf-fe109b255eaa" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{7\\pi}{6}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321898/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "db1ca8dc-ee50-5109-95c9-e3c56aa97366" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321898/field-1/0a6ddc2b5a7aa53dbaf860b36b1154868d90594d50efab51f97b669902110496" :answer-field/choices ["q-321898/field-1/0a6ddc2b5a7aa53dbaf860b36b1154868d90594d50efab51f97b669902110496"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321898" :question/id #uuid "c1a116a1-5be2-57cd-ab23-bacb48cabc85" :question/math-academy-id "q-321898" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/b07f18c13e3bca94d2b55d61b4a63b2a294d0e47ed8a2853f5e10c5140047b27.png)\n\nGiven that the ray above passes through the point with Cartesian coordinates $(-3\\sqrt{3},-3),$ find the polar equation of the ray. Assume that the polar angle is in the range $[0,2\\pi ).$\n\n$\\theta =$\n{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "First, we find the reference angle associated with the point:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\theta }_{R} & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{y}{x}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡|\\frac{-3}{-3\\sqrt{3}}| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, notice that the ray lies in the third quadrant. So, we find the angle in the third quadrant that has a reference angle ${\\theta }_{R}=\\frac{\\pi }{6},$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\theta  & =\\pi +{\\theta }_{R} \\\\  & =\\pi +\\frac{\\pi }{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the polar equation of the ray is \n\n$$\n\\theta =\\frac{7\\pi }{6}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-321898/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "d90b9572-cdac-51f7-b386-81b750642585"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-321898"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-321384/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer/id #uuid "7edd8c0e-8e59-571a-a4e3-20a186958b60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{5}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321384/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818" :answer/id #uuid "ac3e5c0e-011f-5839-b56d-99e4aa68acd6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-321384/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "b65a82ee-d706-5de7-96a5-d41f5b94957d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-321384/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" :answer-field/choices ["q-321384/field-1/8de7a84a41666d4612460439d17949f75cc9ba4883ff75d5034a1786c2a06792" "q-321384/field-1/c43b27454cd69f1b6f4b793e211f4f4f6e40314b87f5b1c35a69172a60fcd818"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-321384" :question/id #uuid "e6c959a6-46d2-5e2c-9bea-847c805ea0c6" :question/math-academy-id "q-321384" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14040587/assets/afa5a80d73d9d8511cc35804277ad9dc3f